  {
   "index": 60,
   "tag": "p×2",
   "landmarks": [
    "article",
    "main"
   ],
   "textLength": 297,
   "text": "I’ve been talking a lot in this post about what I learned from using Tailwind,\nand that’s all true.\nBut I read this post 3 years ago called Tailwind and the Femininity of CSS\nthat really stuck with me. I honestly probably started out with an attitude\ntowards CSS a little like that post describes:",
   "counts": {
    "links": 1,
    "images": 0,
    "headings": 0,
    "listItems": 0,
    "tableRows": 0,
    "controls": 0,
    "paragraphs": 2,
    "repeats": 2,
    "coverLinks": 0
   },
   "linkTextRatio": 0.11,
   "geometry": {
