  {
   "index": 62,
   "tag": "p×4",
   "landmarks": [
    "article",
    "main"
   ],
   "textLength": 1123,
   "text": "But in the last 10 years I’ve learned to really love and respect CSS as a\ntechnology.\nSo I decided years ago that I wanted to react to “CSS is hard” by getting\nbetter at CSS and taking it seriously as a technology, instead of devaluing it.\nDoing that changed everything for me: I learned that so many of my frustrations\n(“centering is impossible”) had been addressed in CSS a long time ago, and that\n",
